# Knovra Sensitive Data Scanner — allowlist
#
# Read docs/GIT_RULES.md §6 before adding anything here.
#
# Each non-comment line is a path fragment or literal string. A staged line is skipped
# when its file path OR its content contains that fragment.
#
# Rules for using this file:
#   - It is for REVIEWED FALSE POSITIVES only. Never for a real credential.
#   - Prefer the narrower `knovra:allow-secret` trailing comment on the single offending line.
#   - Every entry must name WHY it is safe, in a comment directly above it.
#   - Every entry must be justified again in the pull request that adds it.
#   - Broad fragments (a whole directory, a common word) defeat the gate and will be rejected.
#
# Example of an acceptable entry:
#   # Documented local-only Docker Compose default; never used outside infra/docker.
#   infra/docker/docker-compose.yml
